{"name":"Orange Mousse","hex":"#ffbd8a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"orange","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An evergreen tree of the genus Citrus such as Citrus sinensis which yields oranges (the fruit).","Any round citrus fruit with a yellow-red colour when ripe and a sour-sweet taste; the fruit of the orange tree.\n Specifically, a sweet orange or Citrus sinensis."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the colour of the fruit of an orange tree; yellowred; reddish-yellow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/orange"},{"term":"mousse","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An airy pudding served chilled, particularly chocolate mousse.","A savory dish, of meat or seafood, containing gelatin."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To apply mousse (styling cream)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mousse"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mousse","blocks":[{"text":"A mousse is a soft, prepared food that incorporates air bubbles to give it a light and airy texture. It can range from light and fluffy to creamy and thick. A mousse may be sweet or savory."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Chocolate_coffee_mousse.jpg/330px-Chocolate_coffee_mousse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mousse","wikidata":"Q624004"},{"title":"Orange (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Orange is the colour between yellow and red on the spectrum of visible light. The human eyes perceive orange when observing light with a dominant wavelength between roughly 585 and 620 nanometres. In traditional colour theory, it is a secondary colour of pigments, produced by mixing yellow and red. In the RGB colour model, it is a tertiary colour. It is named after the fruit of the same name."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Delicatearch.png/330px-Delicatearch.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&